To apply a Gaussian filter followed by Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you can first define the size and standard deviation of the Gaussian filter kernel. Then, convolve the input grayscale image with the Gaussian filter and apply the Sobel operators on the smoothed image. Here's the modified code:

```matlab
% Load input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');

% Convert to grayscale and resize for faster computation
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
gray_image = imresize(gray_image, [512 512]);

% Define Gaussian filter parameters
sigma = 3;
size_filter = 2*round(sigma*sqrt(2))+1;
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', size_filter, sigma);

% Apply Gaussian filter to input image
smoothed_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter, 'replicate');

% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operators to smoothed image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_x, 'same');
edge_image_y = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions and normalize to display
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
edge_image = (edge_image-min(edge_image(:)))/(max(edge_image(:))-min(edge_image(:)));

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

